{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Pass through, etc.</b> The sense: to proclaim good to the land, for the mourners of Zion, that they may rejoice without fear. Now he returns to explain that Israel's departure from their exile and their return to their land will be in glory, and so the officers of the nations shall say. And the sense of <b>pass through the gates</b> is to proclaim at every single gate, saying: Clear the way of the people, stone it [remove stones from it], raise a standard in the world."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 62, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:00:41.011900989Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}